      "side": 1,
      "message": "I ran some perf tests. Results are in https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mks5OWvfBQUuOtGcowaiHfTtY4q1iYfn4PDiZRTJ7Xo/edit#heading\u003dh.vg8aiu44gss0. \n\nI will run with more iterations but so far it\u0027s looking good I think. This is the increase in serialization/deserialization time:\n\n1. small bundle with basic \u0026 custom types: 1.9%\n2. small bundle with only basic types: 0.1%\n3. large bundle with basic \u0026 custom types: 1.3%\n\nThat is executing the code here but toggling the return of isLengthPrefixed() as always returning false or returning true for the custom types (as it is in this CL).\n\nNote the we also save some bytes from deserialization because we don\u0027t eagerly deserialize everything on the bundle on first touch now. That\u0027s also in the doc. On a sdk_gphone_x86_64_arm64 a few minutes after boot roughly 10% of bytes from **custom-type items** in Bundle are not deserialized with the change.\n",
